[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3717247048","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114669#issuecomment-3717247048","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114669","id":3717247048,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dkLBI","user":{"login":"jackthepunished","id":107313375,"node_id":"U_kgDOBmV43w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/107313375?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished","html_url":"https://github.com/jackthepunished","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-07T04:11:19Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T04:11:19Z","body":"Switched to ResourceLoader::get_resource_type for checking if the deleted file is a resource.\r\nNow clears history for all animations in the player, not just the assigned one.\r\nAdded signal disconnection in NOTIFICATION_EXIT_TREE.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3717247048/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3717399274","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114669#issuecomment-3717399274","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114669","id":3717399274,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dkwLq","user":{"login":"jackthepunished","id":107313375,"node_id":"U_kgDOBmV43w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/107313375?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished","html_url":"https://github.com/jackthepunished","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-07T05:40:40Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T05:40:40Z","body":"> I think this is the wrong way to fix it.\r\n> \r\n> The ghosting issue with undo fundamentally doesn't depend on the AnimationPlayerEditor. If you remove the AnimationPlayer in your MRP, and directly swap the Sprite2D texture, and delete previous texture and performing undo, ghosting should still appear there.\r\n> \r\n> Therefore, handling undoredo solely within the AnimationPlayerEditor is at least misguided. If you want to eliminate ghosting, a fundamental implementation change is likely required.\r\n\r\nThanks for the feedback.\r\nTo fix this at the root level, I propose the following changes:\r\n\r\nAdd a method void invalidate_reference(const Ref<RefCounted> &p_ref) that iterates through the undo/redo history and nullifies any operations holding this specific reference.\r\n\r\nConnect to FileSystemDock::file_removed. When a file is removed, check if it exists in ResourceCache. If it does, retrieve the Ref<Resource> and call invalidate_reference on all active undo histories.\r\n\r\nI believe this would ensure that deleting a file immediately sanitizes the undo history globally, preventing any ghost dependencies.\r\n\r\nSince this is my first PR for a open source project, any feedback is valuable\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3717399274/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3717419160","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114669#issuecomment-3717419160","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114669","id":3717419160,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dk1CY","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-07T05:51:00Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T05:51:00Z","body":"> Connect to FileSystemDock::file_removed\r\n\r\nDoes this mean connecting an UndoRedo object to it? If that's the goal, I think you'll need to change the PR title.\r\n\r\nAlso, since UID was recently implemented, I believe you need to handle it not only in FileSystemDock but also when resources are deleted externally. Regarding how to handle UndoRedo, I think it's better to hear @KoBeWi opinion.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3717419160/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3717438968","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114669#issuecomment-3717438968","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114669","id":3717438968,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dk534","user":{"login":"jackthepunished","id":107313375,"node_id":"U_kgDOBmV43w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/107313375?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished","html_url":"https://github.com/jackthepunished","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-07T06:01:23Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T06:01:23Z","body":"> > Connect to FileSystemDock::file_removed\r\n> \r\n> Does this mean connecting an UndoRedo object to it? If that's the goal, I think you'll need to change the PR title.\r\n> \r\n> Also, since UID was recently implemented, I believe you need to handle it not only in FileSystemDock but also when resources are deleted externally. Regarding how to handle UndoRedo, I think it's better to hear @KoBeWi opinion.\r\n\r\nYou are absolutely right that relying solely on FileSystemDock would miss external file deletions, which is a critical case given the recent UID implementation.\r\n\r\nTo address this comprehensively, I decided to implement a file_removedsignal directly in EditorFileSystem. Since EditorFileSystem is the authority on file scanning and change detection, hooking into it ensures we catch both internal deletions and external deletions.\r\n\r\nMy approach would be:\r\nAdding a file_removed signal to EditorFileSystem first,\r\nHave EditorUndoRedoManager connect to this signal. \r\nWhen a file removal is detected, EditorUndoRedoManager will call UndoRedo::invalidate_reference() to sanitize the history.\r\n\r\nPR title can be changed with the approved approach.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3717438968/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3717485521","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114669#issuecomment-3717485521","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114669","id":3717485521,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dlFPR","user":{"login":"jackthepunished","id":107313375,"node_id":"U_kgDOBmV43w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/107313375?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished","html_url":"https://github.com/jackthepunished","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-07T06:20:56Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T06:20:56Z","body":"Regarding the reimport/revert capability: \r\n\r\nMy implementation explicitly invalidates the reference in UndoHistory to prevent the 'Ghost Dependency' errors and memory leaks. This means if a file is deleted and then re-imported, the Undo history won't automatically restore the link, as it has been sanitized to avoid crashes.\r\n\r\nI believe this trade-off is necessary to fix the reported bug, as keeping the reference alive is exactly what causes the issue.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3717485521/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3717540014","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114669#issuecomment-3717540014","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114669","id":3717540014,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dlSiu","user":{"login":"jackthepunished","id":107313375,"node_id":"U_kgDOBmV43w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/107313375?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished","html_url":"https://github.com/jackthepunished","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackthepunished/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-07T06:40:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T06:40:38Z","body":"I've revised my approach to use a suspend/restore mechanism: when a file is deleted, UndoRedo::suspend_reference(path) releases the reference but keeps the path stored. When the file is reimported, UndoRedo::restore_reference(path, new_ref) reconnects it. This way, ghost dependencies are prevented AND reimport restoration works as you suggested.\r\n\r\nI'm now connecting to EditorFileSystem::file_removed (handles both internal & external deletions) and resources_reimported signals instead of FileSystemDock.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3717540014/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]